# ClipFlow Download System Documentation



This document explains the unified download command system implemented for ClipFlow.

---

## 1. Files Modified / Involved

1. **`backend/src/services/command-generator.service.ts`**
   - Implements `generatePowerShellWorkflow(options)`.
   - Generates exact `yt-dlp` commands for video clips, full videos, and MP3 audio clips with bitrate selection.
   - Formats start/end timestamps from clip editor into `*HH:MM:SS-HH:MM:SS`.
   - Selects the exact quality fallback chain `-f "bestvideo[height<=H]+bestaudio/best[height<=H]"`.
   - Emits `--force-keyframes-at-cuts` and `--js-runtimes node`.

2. **`backend/src/routes/video.routes.ts`**
   - Receives `/download` POST requests with `url`, `format`, `quality`, `audioQuality` / `audioBitrate`, `trimStart`, `trimEnd`, and `customFileName`.
   - Writes the exact workflow command to a temporary `.ps1` file (`clipflow_<timestamp>.ps1`).
   - Executes via `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File <script.ps1>` to prevent Windows `cmd.exe` from mangling format operators `<` and `>`.

3. **`frontend/src/pages/ClipFlowEditor.tsx`**
   - Sends exact start/end seconds, selected video quality (e.g. 1080p, 720p, 4K), audio format (MP4 / MP3 / WAV), and audio bitrates (`0` for best VBR, `320k`, `256k`, `192k`, `128k`).
   - Provides bitrate toggle buttons when MP3 is selected.

4. **`backend/test-commands.mjs`**
   - Automated test suite verifying all combinations of video qualities, MP3 bitrates, time sections, full video downloads, and filename sanitization.

---

## 2. Command Specifications Implemented

### A. Video Clip Download (MP4 with specific resolution)
```powershell
.\yt-dlp.exe `
  --js-runtimes node `
  --download-sections "*00:01:20-00:01:45" `
  -f "bestvideo[height<=1080]+bestaudio/best[height<=1080]" `
  --merge-output-format mp4 `
  --force-keyframes-at-cuts `
  --no-playlist `
  -o "$env:USERPROFILE\Downloads\filename_clip.mp4" `
  "https://youtu.be/4cf5OlJ7bzw"
```

**Quality mapping implemented:**
- **4K / 2160p**: `-f "bestvideo[height<=2160]+bestaudio/best[height<=2160]"`
- **1440p / 2K**: `-f "bestvideo[height<=1440]+bestaudio/best[height<=1440]"`
- **1080p**: `-f "bestvideo[height<=1080]+bestaudio/best[height<=1080]"`
- **720p**: `-f "bestvideo[height<=720]+bestaudio/best[height<=720]"`
- **480p**: `-f "bestvideo[height<=480]+bestaudio/best[height<=480]"`
- **360p**: `-f "bestvideo[height<=360]+bestaudio/best[height<=360]"`
- **240p**: `-f "bestvideo[height<=240]+bestaudio/best[height<=240]"`
- **Best**: `-f "bestvideo+bestaudio/best"`

---

### B. MP3 Audio Clip (with exact start/end trim)
```powershell
.\yt-dlp.exe `
  --js-runtimes node `
  --download-sections "*00:01:20-00:01:45" `
  -x `
  --audio-format mp3 `
  --audio-quality 0 `
  --force-keyframes-at-cuts `
  --no-playlist `
  -o "$env:USERPROFILE\Downloads\filename_clip.mp3" `
  "https://youtu.be/4cf5OlJ7bzw"
```

**Audio quality options supported:**
- `--audio-quality 0` (Best VBR conversion quality)
- `--audio-quality 320K` (320 kbps)
- `--audio-quality 256K` (256 kbps)
- `--audio-quality 192K` (192 kbps)
- `--audio-quality 128K` (128 kbps)

---

### C. Full Video / Full MP3 (When no trim range is specified)
Omits `--download-sections` and `--force-keyframes-at-cuts`, downloading the entire stream directly in one pass.

---

## 3. Key Enhancements & Fixes Applied

1. **`--force-keyframes-at-cuts` Added**:
   Ensures video and audio cuts begin on an exact I-frame boundary for clean start times without black frames or audio sync delay.

2. **`--js-runtimes node` Added**:
   Uses the local Node.js environment to evaluate YouTube player Javascript challenges without throttling.

3. **No Mangling via `cmd.exe`**:
   PowerShell commands containing `<` and `>` in `-f "bestvideo[height<=1080]..."` are executed cleanly from a standalone script file so Windows Command Prompt does not treat them as redirection operators.

4. **Output Destination**:
   Saved to `$env:USERPROFILE\Downloads\<customName_or_title>_clip.<ext>`. Invalid Windows filename characters (`<`, `>`, `:`, `"`, `/`, `\`, `|`, `?`, `*`) are automatically sanitized.


